# Far JMP (EA ptr16:16/32, FF /5 m16:16/32). The caller substitutes the
# target reader, which defines target_value and selector; a memory pointer
# is read whole before the transfer. far_jump (privilege.rs) takes a code
# segment at CPL or a call gate to one; it never changes the level.
require_width 16_or_32
# V86 mode (VM=1) is not modelled yet.
read_flags entry
bit vm entry 17
not no_vm vm
require no_vm
$FAR_TARGET
zext target32 target_value 32
far_jump selector target32
preserve_flags all
retire
